            "summary": "{{ if $values }}A realm-server process reached 15+ concurrent _search / _federated-search computations at least once in the last 5 minutes (baseline is single digits). Sourced from the periodic health line (inFlightSearch=N: admission slots, which counts both routes — including the in-render _search round-trips prerender issues — but not requests the live-search cache answers from another computation; searchRequests=N counts those too). Concurrent search load drives heap growth toward OOM — this is the early-warning signal; find which client/realm is issuing the searches.{{ else }}Grafana could not run this rule's query. This is the rule's DatasourceError alert, and its Error annotation gives the reason. It shows nothing about search load. The query reads CloudWatch: the Error annotation's text says why, usually throttling or a missing permission.{{ end }}"
