            "summary": "{{ if $values }}A database session of the realm-server's role was blocked acquiring an advisory lock for more than 10 minutes at some point in the last 5 minutes. Sourced from dbAdvisoryWaitMaxMs on the periodic health line, read from pg_stat_activity (wait_event 'advisory') on a connection of the probe's own every 30s; dbAdvisoryWaiters on the same line counts the blocked sessions. Each one holds a pooled connection while it waits, so enough of them starve the pool. A writer waits as long as the holder keeps the lock: a realm publish holds it for up to about 7 minutes on production, which the threshold sits above. The holder is the session the waiters queue behind: in pg_locks it holds the granted advisory lock with the waiters' classid/objid, and it is usually idle in transaction.{{ else }}Grafana could not run this rule's query. This is the rule's DatasourceError alert, and its Error annotation gives the reason. It shows nothing about advisory lock waits. The query reads CloudWatch: the Error annotation's text says why, usually throttling or a missing permission.{{ end }}"
